<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Documentation on Gate One</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/</link><description>Recent content in Documentation on Gate One</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Components and installation</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/install/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/install/</guid><description>&lt;div id="preamble"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Gate One is one binary in front of your applications. Everything else —&#10;an identity provider, the optional broker, the token broker, Redis — is a&#10;separate component you choose to run.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sect1"&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="the-components"&gt;The components&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch"&gt;&#10;&lt;colgroup&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 16.6666%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 33.3333%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 33.3333%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 16.6668%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&#10;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Component&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Role&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Shipped as&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Required?&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gate One&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;The gateway: route policy, session, proxy, MCP, injection&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Signed release binary &lt;code&gt;gate-one&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;yes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity provider&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Identification and (optionally) authorization claims&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;External (Keycloak, Entra ID, Auth0, …)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;yes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reverse proxy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;TLS termination, routing, load balancing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;External (Traefik, nginx, Caddy, …)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;recommended&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;cladone-auth&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Optional embedded IAM / OIDC issuer (IdP federation, grants)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Signed release binary &lt;code&gt;cladone-auth&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;optional&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Token broker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Per-user delegated credentials for upstream calls&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Source &lt;code&gt;services/token-broker&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;optional&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;auth-bridge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Reference implementation of the &lt;code&gt;http-bridge&lt;/code&gt; contract&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Source &lt;code&gt;services/auth-bridge&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;optional&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Redis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Shared session/revocation state for several replicas&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;External (Sentinel)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;only for HA&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;All releases attach a single &lt;code&gt;services_&amp;lt;version&amp;gt;_src.tar.gz&lt;/code&gt; containing&#10;the token broker and auth-bridge sources. They are &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; part of the&#10;&lt;code&gt;gate-one&lt;/code&gt; binary: each runs as its own container.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>IAM, IdPs and provider types</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/iam-and-providers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/iam-and-providers/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IAM&lt;/strong&gt; services cover authorization and configure the identity providers (&lt;strong&gt;IdPs&lt;/strong&gt;) they trust.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Gate One sits between the user, an IAM/authorization source and an IdP.&#10;The schema&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;authProvider.type&lt;/code&gt; is a &lt;strong&gt;provider type&lt;/strong&gt;: it selects who&#10;Gate One asks to verify a request and obtain identity/authorization&#10;claims. It is not an IAM by itself.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Architecture</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/architecture/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/architecture/</guid><description>&lt;div id="preamble"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Gate One is a reverse proxy at the edge. It authenticates the request,&#10;applies route policy, optionally injects UX, then forwards the request&#10;to the existing application. The application keeps its own URL, stack&#10;and deployment; it does not need an SDK.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>HTTP bridge contract</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/bridge-contract/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/bridge-contract/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;authProvider.type: &amp;quot;http-bridge&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt; delegates request verification to an&#10;external HTTP service: the &lt;strong&gt;bridge&lt;/strong&gt;. The bridge adapts a technology&#10;Gate One does not implement natively — SAML, LDAP, mTLS, API keys, a&#10;legacy session service — to three small endpoints and a login page.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Plugins</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/plugins/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/plugins/</guid><description>&lt;div id="preamble"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Gate One extensions are &lt;strong&gt;out-of-process&lt;/strong&gt; services. The gateway talks&#10;to them over HTTP/JSON; it never loads a third-party authentication&#10;provider and never calls a plugin on the authentication path.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sect1"&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="plugin-families"&gt;Plugin families&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch"&gt;&#10;&lt;colgroup&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 33.3333%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 16.6666%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 16.6666%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 16.6666%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 16.6669%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&#10;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Family&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Runs in&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Transport&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Decides auth?&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Licence&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Auth adapter&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;broker&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;HTTP/JSON (gRPC later)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;yes, in the broker&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Gate One licence&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Injection / userscript / UI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Gate One&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;route &lt;code&gt;inject&lt;/code&gt; bundle (config)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;no&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;extension licence&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Event consumer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Gate One&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;HTTP/JSON, signed manifest&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;no&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;extension licence&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The injection bundle and the event consumer are extensions; auth adapters&#10;stay in the broker and remain under the Gate One licence.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;Backend-For-Frontend is not a plugin&lt;/strong&gt;: it is a proxied &lt;code&gt;backend:&lt;/code&gt;&#10;route, post-auth by definition (it receives the identity DTO /&#10;&lt;code&gt;X-Gate-One-Subject&lt;/code&gt;), and can be written in any language. Gate One&#10;never loads it. Response transforms are the gateway’s native injector&#10;chain (&lt;code&gt;inject&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;rewriteBody&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;responseHeaders&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;rewriteRedirects&lt;/code&gt;,&#10;the guard); bespoke logic belongs in the backend or the edge proxy, not&#10;in a plugin.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Publish and trust a plugin</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/publish-a-plugin/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/publish-a-plugin/</guid><description>&lt;div id="preamble"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Gate One extensions are &lt;strong&gt;out-of-process services&lt;/strong&gt;. They are trusted&#10;through a &lt;strong&gt;signed manifest&lt;/strong&gt; and a local &lt;strong&gt;trust store&lt;/strong&gt;; code is never&#10;loaded into the gateway. This page is the publisher/operator walkthrough:&#10;develop, sign, install and revoke.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sect1"&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="plugin-families"&gt;Plugin families&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch"&gt;&#10;&lt;colgroup&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 20%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 40%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 20%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;col style="width: 20%;"/&gt;&#10;&lt;/colgroup&gt;&#10;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Family&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Contract&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Signed&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;th class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;Status&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Event consumer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET /health&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;POST /events&lt;/code&gt; (HTTP/JSON)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;manifest, &lt;code&gt;capabilities: [&amp;#34;events&amp;#34;]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;implemented&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Injection / UI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;code&gt;route.inject&lt;/code&gt; bundle (&lt;code&gt;inject-bundle.schema.json&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;route config, not a signed plugin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;implemented&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Auth adapter&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;broker only&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kind: auth&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="tableblock halign-left valign-top"&gt;&lt;p class="tableblock"&gt;Gate One licence, not an extension&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Only the &lt;strong&gt;event consumer&lt;/strong&gt; is a fully signed extension today.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;Backend-For-Frontend is not a plugin&lt;/strong&gt;: it is a proxied &lt;code&gt;backend:&lt;/code&gt;&#10;route, post-auth by definition, written in any language. Response&#10;transforms are the gateway’s native injector chain (&lt;code&gt;inject&lt;/code&gt;,&#10;&lt;code&gt;rewriteBody&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;responseHeaders&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;rewriteRedirects&lt;/code&gt;, the guard); bespoke&#10;logic belongs in the backend or the edge proxy.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Token broker</title><link>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/token-broker/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/token-broker/</guid><description>&lt;div id="preamble"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="sectionbody"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The token broker is the optional companion service behind&#10;&lt;a href="https://clad-one.github.io/gate-one-doc/v0.4.5-docs.1/docs/features/delegated-credentials/"&gt;Delegated credentials&lt;/a&gt;. It&#10;holds a registry of OAuth 2.0 providers and an encrypted &lt;strong&gt;per-user&lt;/strong&gt;&#10;token store, and hands Gate One the access token of one authenticated&#10;user for one provider.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="paragraph"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It is deliberately &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; an identity provider and &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; a reverse&#10;proxy: Gate One keeps its own identity; the broker only obtains and&#10;stores the user’s token for an upstream service.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>